   "title": "README: H3 LongTake character swap v2 (Character Swap LoRA)",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 LongTake: character swap v2 (Character Swap LoRA)\n\nThe person in the source video is replaced by the character of `<Picture 1>`, keeping room, motion and camera of `<Video 1>`.\n\n**What is different from the v1 workflow**\n- The [Character Swap LoRA by akatz-ai](https://huggingface.co/akatz-ai/MiniMax-H3-Character-Swap-LoRA) (`h3_character_swap_pro4500_1000.safetensors` in `models/loras`, strength 1.0) with the **Turbo 8-step 768p** LoRA, `res_multistep` / `simple`, 8 steps: the configuration the LoRA author tested. Plus **shift 10/3**, our setting for a 0.5 MP base.\n- The LoRA works best on 4-5 s shots: those are our clips, each one gets its own slice of the source as `<Video 1>`.\n- **A close-up of the face as `<Picture 2>`** (`ref_image_2`): measured +0.04-0.05 likeness at no cost. A multi-view sheet as `<Picture 3>` gave nothing more on our test.\n- **`source_face = blur_keep_mouth`** on the Render: the face of the person in the `<Video 1>` slice is blurred except the mouth, so the identity comes from your pictures only and lip sync survives. It matters when the source person's identity leaks into the result (measured: likeness to the character 0.41 -> 0.52, to the source person 0.41 -> 0.22); with a character very different from the source person it changes little. `blur` blurs the mouth too (still mouth: dances, gestures). Needs insightface.\n\n**Prompt**: the formula the LoRA was trained on, \"Replace only <who, with a visible detail> in <Video 1> with the character in <Picture 1>: ...\". Name the target by something visible (\"the man in the purple shirt\"), describe hair, distinctive face traits and outfit, **no expression instructions** (they can switch the swap off). See *Character swap* in `docs/PROMPTING.md` for an instruction you can give an LLM to write it.\n\n**Measured** on a 14 s TikTok (3 clips), against the v1 workflow with a head-swap LoRA: background twice as faithful (difference 34 -> 18), likeness 0.21 -> 0.32 with the face close-up, same motion; the bag and top of the character appear, and nothing of the source person's necklace remains.\n\nSometimes a clip changes only the clothes and keeps the old face: redo that clip (`mode = redo_one`, `redo_from_clip`) with another seed.\n\nSteps: `dry_run=true` -> `max_clips=2` -> `max_clips=0` -> Ctrl+M on the Stitch."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## H3 LongTake: character swap v2 (Character Swap LoRA)\n\nThe person in the source video is replaced by the character of `<Picture 1>`, keeping room, motion and camera of `<Video 1>`.\n\n**What is different from the v1 workflow**\n- The [Character Swap LoRA by akatz-ai](https://huggingface.co/akatz-ai/MiniMax-H3-Character-Swap-LoRA) (`h3_character_swap_pro4500_1000.safetensors` in `models/loras`, strength 1.0) with the **Turbo 8-step 768p** LoRA, `res_multistep` / `simple`, 8 steps: the configuration the LoRA author tested. Plus **shift 10/3**, our setting for a 0.5 MP base.\n- The LoRA works best on 4-5 s shots: those are our clips, each one gets its own slice of the source as `<Video 1>`.\n- **A close-up of the face as `<Picture 2>`** (`ref_image_2`): measured +0.04-0.05 likeness at no cost. A multi-view sheet as `<Picture 3>` gave nothing more on our test.\n- **`source_face = blur_keep_mouth`** on the Render: the face of the person in the `<Video 1>` slice is blurred except the mouth, so the identity comes from your pictures only and lip sync survives. It matters when the source person's identity leaks into the result (measured: likeness to the character 0.41 -> 0.52, to the source person 0.41 -> 0.22); with a character very different from the source person it changes little. `blur` blurs the mouth too (still mouth: dances, gestures). Needs insightface.\n\n**Prompt**: the formula the LoRA was trained on, \"Replace only <who, with a visible detail> in <Video 1> with the character in <Picture 1>: ...\". Name the target by something visible (\"the man in the purple shirt\"), describe hair, distinctive face traits and outfit, **no expression instructions** (they can switch the swap off). See *Character swap* in `docs/PROMPTING.md` for an instruction you can give an LLM to write it.\n\n**Measured** on a 14 s TikTok (3 clips), against the v1 workflow with a head-swap LoRA: background twice as faithful (difference 34 -> 18), likeness 0.21 -> 0.32 with the face close-up, same motion; the bag and top of the character appear, and nothing of the source person's necklace remains.\n\nSometimes a clip changes only the clothes and keeps the old face: redo that clip (`mode = redo_one`, `redo_from_clip`) with another seed.\n\nSteps: `dry_run=true` -> `max_clips=2` -> `max_clips=0` -> Ctrl+M on the Stitch."
   },
